Subject: [EXPERIMENTAL] prima: start cfg80211 scheduled scanning immediately

Android can start scheduled scanning while the display is off but before the
host enters suspend (for example, while connected over USB). Waiting for a
host suspend transition can leave saved-network discovery idle. Keep the
requested intervals and use the firmware's existing IMMEDIATE mode.

Not runtime-tested. This does not fix the separate NV-download timeout.

--- a/drivers/staging/prima/CORE/HDD/src/wlan_hdd_cfg80211.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/prima/CORE/HDD/src/wlan_hdd_cfg80211.c
@@ -7306,7 +7306,7 @@ static int wlan_hdd_cfg80211_sched_scan_start(struct wiphy *wiphy,
     pPnoRequest->scanTimers.aTimerValues[0].uTimerValue =
           (request->interval)/1000;
     pPnoRequest->scanTimers.aTimerValues[0].uTimerRepeat = 0;
-    pPnoRequest->modePNO = SIR_PNO_MODE_ON_SUSPEND;
+    pPnoRequest->modePNO = SIR_PNO_MODE_IMMEDIATE;
 
     status = sme_SetPreferredNetworkList(WLAN_HDD_GET_HAL_CTX(pAdapter),
                               pPnoRequest, pAdapter->sessionId,
